 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? That's common stuck point. Have you tried the conversation exchanges at French cafes? It can be, but lots of people start there. Sit with a friend at cafe where people are talking loudly, and copy what they say. After a while, you'll pick up phrases. It is, but walking around town while listening to people speak is the best way to learn any language. You could also try an app like Duolingo. A native speaker, usually. They're usually quite happy to help, and it' good for them too. Great idea. write down what you hear, and read French books and newspapers every day. You' be surprised how quickly it clicks.",
